message.content:
Garden rakes fall under heading 8201 (hand tools: spades, shovels, mattocks, picks, hoes, forks and rakes). Subheading 8201.30 covers mattocks, picks, hoes and rakes, and 8201.30.00 is the 8-digit line. The statistical suffix is 8201.30.0000. The item is a rake with a scoop function, made of plastic and aluminum. Heading 8201 does not limit the base material of the tool, and Note 1 to Chapter 82 says the chapter covers tools with working parts of base metal. Here the working parts are plastic, so classification in 8201 is arguable.

The alternative is heading 3926 (other articles of plastics), specifically 3926.90. Chapter 82 Note 1 covers only tools with working parts of base metal, or of other materials if the tool is metal-mounted. Since the working parts are plastic panels on an aluminum pole, Note 1 may exclude the item. Yet CBP has ruled on plastic leaf scoops/hand rakes, often classifying them under 3926.90.9990 (or under 8201.30 for plastic-tined rakes with metal handles). Rakes with plastic heads and metal handles are commonly classified in 8201.30.0000, because the handle is metal and the tool's essential character comes from the combined article. Heading 8201 also notes in Note 1 that tools with working parts of other materials are included if they have a base metal handle or mounting. I'll go with 8201.30.0000.

{"hts_code": "8201.30.0000", "reason": "A hand-operated garden rake with an aluminum pole and handle and plastic rake and scoop panels is classified as a rake in heading 8201, subheading 8201.30."}
